---
layout: changelog
title: Deploy server-rendered sites from npm, pnpm, and Bun workspaces
date: 2026-11-10
cover: /images/blog/announcing-monorepo-support-for-sites/cover.avif
tags: sites
---

Appwrite Sites can now deploy server-rendered apps straight from a monorepo. The site's root directory stays at the root of the repository (`./`), the build command builds just your app, such as `pnpm --filter web build`, and the output directory points at that app's build output, such as `./apps/web/.next`.

- npm, pnpm, and Bun workspaces are all supported.
- It works with every JavaScript SSR framework: Next.js, Nuxt, Astro, SvelteKit, Remix, TanStack Start, Angular, and Analog.
- Deployments include the workspace packages your app imports and leave the repo's other apps out.
- Next.js standalone output works inside a monorepo too.
- Nuxt and Remix apps installed with pnpm now deploy correctly in single-app repos as well.

Self-hosted Appwrite picks this up after pulling the latest image for your build runtime, such as `openruntimes/node:v5-22`, and redeploying.

